-- title:
--   From HTo G G Hat Tuple Outcome Tail Snoc
-- statement:
--   **Removing the first completed outcome from a snoc tuple commutes with snoc.**
--
--   Let $gs$ be a tuple of $n+1$ completed slice outcomes and let $g$ be one further completed slice outcome. Write $\operatorname{tail}(gs)$ for deletion of the first outcome and use $\operatorname{snoc}$ to append an outcome.
--
--   Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{tail}\!\left(\operatorname{snoc}(gs,g)\right)
--   =\operatorname{snoc}\!\left(\operatorname{tail}(gs),g\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the outcome-tuple counterpart of the point-tuple identity and is used in the snoc recursion for the ordered G-hat half-product.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
